@page
@model SavingsAcc
@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Savings Account";
}

<section class="section">
    <div class="container">
        <div class="divider">Savings Accounts</div>
        <h3>Savings Options Tailored to You</h3>
        <p style="max-width:640px;">We offer flexible account types so every member of our community can start building a financial cushion:</p>
    </div>
</section>

<section class="section section-alt">
    <div class="container">
        <div class="grid grid-3" style="align-items:start;">
            <div class="card">
                <h3>Regular Savings Account</h3>
                <p>Our standard passbook account for individuals, joint accounts, or families looking for a flexible way to manage daily cash and earn interest.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="card">
                <h3>Basic Deposit Account</h3>
                <p>Perfect for first-time savers, students, and micro-earners with zero maintaining balance and minimal documentation requirements.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="card">
                <h3>In-Trust-For (ITF) Savings Account</h3>
                <p>Set aside money for your children's future education and milestones under a parent's or guardian's management.</p>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>

<section class="section">
    <div class="container">
        <div class="divider">Requirements</div>
        <h3>What You Need to Bring</h3>
        <p style="max-width:640px;">Opening an account is quick and straightforward. Just bring the following to our main office:</p>

        <div class="grid grid-2" style="margin-top:30px;">
            <div class="card">
                <h3>1. Identification Documents</h3>
                <p style="font-size:0.9rem; color:var(--color-soil);">Bring 1 Primary ID</p>
                <ul>
                    <li>Philippine Identification Card (PhilID / ePhilID)</li>
                    <li>Passport</li>
                    <li>Driver's License</li>
                    <li>UMID / SSS / GSIS Card</li>
                    <li>Postal ID or Voter's ID / Certification</li>
                </ul>
                <p style="font-size:0.9rem; margin-top:15px;"><em>For students: School ID with current enrollment photo and Birth Certificate.</em></p>
            </div>
            <div class="card">
                <h3>2. Supporting Items</h3>
                <ul>
                    <li><strong>Proof of Address:</strong> Latest electric or water bill (past 3 months) or Barangay Clearance.</li>
                    <li><strong>Photos:</strong> Two (2) recent 2x2 ID photos.</li>
                    <li><strong>Opening Deposit:</strong> Initial cash deposit to activate your passbook.</li>
                </ul>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>

<section class="section section-alt">
    <div class="container">
        <div class="divider">How to Get Started</div>
        <h3>3 Easy Steps to Open Your Account</h3>

        <div class="grid grid-3" style="margin-top:40px;">
            <div class="card">
                <h3>1. Gather Your Requirements</h3>
                <p style="font-size:0.9rem; color:var(--color-soil); font-weight:600;">Simple documents</p>
                <p>Prepare 1 valid government-issued ID, proof of address, two 2x2 photos, and your initial deposit amount.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="card">
                <h3>2. Visit Rural Bank of Norala</h3>
                <p style="font-size:0.9rem; color:var(--color-soil); font-weight:600;">In-person service</p>
                <p>Drop by our main office. Our friendly Account Officers will help you fill out the Customer Information Sheet (CIS).</p>
            </div>
            <div class="card">
                <h3>3. Receive Your Passbook</h3>
                <p style="font-size:0.9rem; color:var(--color-soil); font-weight:600;">Same-day turnover</p>
                <p>Make your initial deposit at the teller counter and receive your official passbook on the spot.</p>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>

<section class="section">
    <div class="container">
        <div class="divider">Deposit Protection</div>
        <h3>Protected Savings</h3>
        <p style="max-width:640px;">Deposits are insured by the Philippine Deposit Insurance Corporation (PDIC) up to ₱500,000 per depositor. Rural Bank of Norala is proudly supervised by the Bangko Sentral ng Pilipinas (BSP).</p>
    </div>
</section>